<title>CHILE: LAN Chile buys Boeing jets for $300 million.</title>
<headline>LAN Chile buys Boeing jets for $300 million.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO, Chile</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean airline LAN Chile said Wednesday it ordered three new Boeing 767-300 ER jets for $300 million and took an option for two more of the aircraft.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the biggest direct purchase in the history of Chilean civil aviation and it is also the biggest made in the past few years by a Latin American airline, which tend to operate leased fleets,&quot; LAN President Jorge Awad said.</p>
<p>He said LAN will finance the deal with a 12-year loan from the Canadian International Investment Bank.</p>
<p>Boeing Co. stock rose $1.375 to $103.125 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
